083 - O Worship the King
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 83
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[G]O worship [D]the [G]King, all [C/E]glorious [G]above,
[D]Ogratefully [C/E]sing [Bm]His wonderful [G]love;
[D]Our shield and defender, [G/D]the [D]Ancient [G/D]of [D7]days,
[D7]Pavilioned [D]in [G]splendour, [C/E]and [Bm]girded [G/D]with [D7]praise.

Verse 2:
[G]O tell of [D]His [G]might, O [C/E]sing [D7/F#]of [G]His [D]grace,
[D]Whose [G]robe is [D]the [G]light, [C/E]whose [Bm]canopy [D7]space,
[D]His chariots of [D7]wrath the [G/D]deep [D]thunderclouds [D7]form,
[D7]And [G]dark is [D]His [G]path on [C/E]the [Bm]wings of [G/D]the [D7]storm.

Verse 3:
[G]Thy bountiful care, what [C/E]tongue [D7/F#]can [G]recite?
[D]It breathes [G/B]in [D]the [G]air, [C/E]it [Bm]shines [G/D]in [D7]the [G]light;
[D]It streams from the [D7]hills, it [G/D]descends [D]to [G/D]the [D7]plain,
[D7]And [G]sweetly [D]distills [G]in [C/E]the [Bm]dew and [G/D]the [D7]rain.

Verse 4:
[G]Frail children [D]of [G]dust, and [C/E]feeble [G]as [D]frail,
[D]In [G]Thee do [D]we [G]trust, [C/E]nor [Bm]find Thee [G/D]to [D7]fail;
[D]Thy mercies how [D7]tender, [G/D]how [D]firm to [G/D]the [D7]end!
[D7]Our [G]Maker, [D]Defender, [C/E]Redeemer, [G/D]and [D7]Friend.
